  "term": "DS",
  "definition": "DS stands for disulfiram, a medicine used in mental health care to support treatment of alcoholism. It works by blocking the enzyme that breaks down acetaldehyde after alcohol is consumed, causing acetaldehyde to build up and trigger an intensely unpleasant reaction.",
